            <ArticleTitle>Effect of quinapril on intimal hyperplasia after coronary stenting as assessed by intravascular ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>443-5, A6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied whether angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibition with quinapril treatment can prevent in-stent restenosis after successful implantation of Palmaz-Schatz stents. Intravascular ultrasound study, but not quantitative coronary angiography analysis, revealed that quinapril treatment significantly prevented the loss of both minimal lumen cross-sectional area and lumen volume in stents, in addition to reducing the increase in intimal hyperplasia volume.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
